with Tyare speakers, it is concluded that the sound change *† &gt; š has initially occurred only after y or i, as a result of partial assimilation, and that it is found in all but four Tyare dialects located in the western and southwestern periphery of Tyare territory.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
